title: Authorizations › Case page › Criteria & risk › Pop-ups
route: /authorizations/case/R-1042?tab=criteria
intro: The three pop-ups on Criteria & risk: the breakdown of the approval chance, the full list of comparable decisions, and how the approval chance is calculated.
dir: TD
---
group gW "See the breakdown"
  click br "Click 'See the breakdown'"
  overlay m0 "Pop-up 'Why 62%'\nthe formula '58 + 4 + 6 + 2 + 0 + 0 − 8 = 62'"
  process bars "Bars: the starting point, six rows, then 'Approval chance now'\na dashed outline for what is still to come\n'Clinical context you added' appears once a note is added"
  process lo "'Likely outcomes'\nApproved as asked 62% · Partly approved 25% · Denied 13%"
  click c0 "Click 'Close'"
endgroup

group gA "See all"
  click sa "Click 'See all' under 'Similar decisions'"
  overlay m1 "Pop-up 'Comparable decisions'\nsix of the closest matches"
  process dy "Outcomes use the request's own days\ne.g. 'Approved 14/14' or 'Approved 7/14'"
  click c1 "Click 'Close'"
endgroup

group gB "How it is calculated"
  click hc "Click 'How it is calculated'"
  overlay m2 "Pop-up 'How the approval chance is calculated'"
  agent s1 "1 Historian finds similar decisions"
  agent s2 "2 Forecaster starts from the base rate"
  process s3 "3 It adds and takes away points\n4 The range says how sure it is"
  agent s5 "5 Forecaster checks it every night"
  click c2 "Click 'Got it'"
endgroup

click cx "Click the X, click the dimmed area, or press Esc"
end e "Pop-up closes\nYou are back on Criteria & risk, nothing changed"

br --> m0 --> bars --> lo --> c0 --> e
m0 --> cx
sa --> m1 --> dy --> c1 --> e
m1 --> cx
hc --> m2 --> s1 --> s2 --> s3 --> s5 --> c2 --> e
m2 --> cx
cx --> e
